linux-nvidia-bos (7.0.0-2025.26) resolute; urgency=medium

  * resolute/linux-nvidia-bos: 7.0.0-2025.26 -proposed tracker (LP: #2174003)

  * coresight etm4x build failure after stable backport of "Set active path on
    target CPU" (LP: #2174422)
    - coresight: Save active path for system tracers

  * linux-nvidia: preserve userspace min_free_kbytes across recalculation
    (LP: #2173855)
    - mm: stop recalculating min_free_kbytes once set by userspace

  * NVIDIA: SAUCE: resctrl/mpam: fix force_unknown_msc sysfs parameter
    (LP: #2173591)
    - NVIDIA: SAUCE: resctrl/mpam: fix force_unknown_msc sysfs parameter

  * Container churn throughput drops ~5x with udev enabled because veth
    publishes and then removes one sysfs queue object per possible CPU
    (LP: #2173592)
    - veth: decide peer queue count from the peer's own attributes
    - NVIDIA: SAUCE: veth: set the real number of queues before registering
      the devices

  * NVIDIA: Backport iommu/smmuv3 fixes for cmdqv teardown (LP: #2173553)
    - iommu/arm-smmu-v3: Disable the impl before disabling the SMMU on
      shutdown

  * Align SMT PE0 prioritization with upstream in linux-nvidia (LP: #2173514)
    - Revert "NVIDIA: VR: SAUCE: sched/fair: Honor asymmetric SMT priority in
      idle selection"
    - Revert "NVIDIA: VR: SAUCE: sched/fair: Prefer fully idle cores for NOHZ
      balancing"
    - Revert "NVIDIA: VR: SAUCE: sched/fair: Add SIS_UTIL support to
      select_idle_capacity()"
    - Revert "NVIDIA: VR: SAUCE: sched/fair: Prefer fully-idle SMT cores in
      asym-capacity idle selection"
    - Revert "NVIDIA: VR: SAUCE: sched/fair: Attach sched_domain_shared to
      sd_asym_cpucapacity"
    - sched/fair: Attach sched_domain_shared to sd_asym_cpucapacity
    - sched/fair: Prefer fully-idle SMT cores in asym-capacity idle selection
    - sched/fair: Add SIS_UTIL support to select_idle_capacity()
    - sched/fair: Prefer fully idle cores for NOHZ balancing
    - sched/fair: Honor asymmetric SMT priority in idle selection
    - sched/fair: Simplify the entry condition for update_idle_cpu_scan()
    - sched/topology: Add asymmetric SMT packing override
    - NVIDIA: VR: SAUCE: sched/topology: Default to SMT packing on arm64

  * NVIDIA: Backport steal governor (LP: #2172891)
    - sched/cputime: Add kcpustat_field_total helper
    - cpumask: Introduce cpumask_intersects_and
    - sched/docs: Document cpu_preferred_mask and Preferred CPU concept
    - cpumask: Introduce cpu_preferred_mask
    - sysfs: Add preferred CPU file
    - sched/core: Try to use a preferred CPU in is_cpu_allowed
    - sched/fair: Load balance only among preferred CPUs
    - sched/core: Push current task from non preferred CPU
    - sched/debug: Add migration stats due to non preferred CPUs
    - virt: Introduce steal governor driver
    - virt/steal_governor: Add control knobs for handling steal values
    - virt/steal_governor: Implement steal_governor policy loop
    - virt/steal_governor: Enable the driver
    - sched/core: Fix context analysis errors in non-preferred CPU push
    - NVIDIA: SAUCE: [Config] Build the steal governor as a module

  * MT8901: USB keyboard or mouse cannot wake the system from s2idle
    (LP: #2172005)
    - NVIDIA: SAUCE: pinctrl: paris: no-op pinmux hooks for virtual GPIOs
    - NVIDIA: SAUCE: pinctrl: mt8901: add virtual GPIOs for EINT 182-208
    - NVIDIA: SAUCE: pinctrl: paris: report no debounce support for EINTs
      without it
    - NVIDIA: SAUCE: usb: xhci-plat: use the ACPI GpioInt as MTK v2 wake IRQ

  * MT8901 lid opening does not wake system from suspend (LP: #2171427)
    - NVIDIA: SAUCE: soc: mediatek: power_wrap: fix lid wake on MT8901

  * spi: tegra210-quad: Improve interrupt handling for loaded systems
    (LP: #2167046)
    - spi: tegra210-quad: Fix false positive WARN on interrupt timeout with
      transfer complete
    - spi: tegra210-quad: Convert to hard IRQ with high-priority workqueue
    - spi: tegra210-quad: Cache TRANS_STATUS in ISR for timeout handler
    - spi: tegra210-quad: Process small PIO transfers in hard IRQ context
    - NVIDIA: SAUCE: spi: tegra210-quad: don't overwrite refreshed status with
      lost-IRQ snapshot

  * ACPI: processor_idle: support hierarchical LPI power states (LP: #2167301)
    - NVIDIA: SAUCE: ACPI: processor_idle: Hold LPI consumer across idle-
      capable hotplug states

  * NVDA8000 USB controllers fail to probe with xhci-hcd NVDA8001:00: Not find
    power wrap config data (LP: #2171975)
    - NVIDIA: SAUCE: usb: xhci-plat: fall back to generic xHCI without Power
      Wrap device control

  * arm_ffa notification ID collision prevents EC service from probing
    (LP: #2171426)
    - NVIDIA: SAUCE: firmware: arm_ffa: Compare notify_id when looking up
      notifier callbacks

  * [linux-nvidia]: hid-asus: brightness hotkeys dead on ASUS laptops with the
    0B05:4B42 I2C keyboard (LP: #2171100)
    - NVIDIA: SAUCE: HID: asus: map Consumer brightness usages on I2C
      keyboards

